  "purpose": "Keep one canonical-prefix- and capacity-compatible in-memory fake-IP pool identity (mutex/store/allocator) across DNS service reloads, for IPv4 and IPv6 separately.",
  "limits": [
    "Not a DNS-response quiescence barrier; does not prove all resolver caches fresh.",
    "Different prefix and backing-kind transitions deliberately retain the upstream clone branch.",
    "Pool wrap/eviction/persistence policy are not redesigned.",
    "Caller must keep the Windows prefix stable and not flush/disable/recreate the live pool during transition.",
    "Only known nonnil memoryStore pools are reused; persistent pools always retain the upstream clone branch because constructor restoreState can clear shared storage before PatchFrom.",
    "Memory capacity must also match exactly; zero-capacity construction semantics are unchanged."
  ],
  "persistence_note": "Only nonpersistent pools are reused. Upstream New(Persistence=true) can call restoreState and clear shared storage before PatchFrom; persistent pools retain the upstream clone branch.",
